## Context
Source: two-auditor review 2026-11-01 (Fable claude-fable-5-1, Astra gpt-6-astra) at 27660f5; report https://claude.ai/artifact/Vk51ZHGtmd2x7rea65yf33. Lines marked (checked) were re-read against the code by the session.
806 raw monitor files (client IPs, 89 with user queries) were committed publicly in tests/fixtures/reports/monitor-logs/ from 2025-10-29 (checked). Removed from the tree and ignored by PR #277 (2026-11-01). The rewritten history is ready; the force-push needs ruleset 5157496 lifted by a CIRED org admin (request sent 2026-11-01). The privacy notice (src/monitor/templates/privacy.html:17) says no personal data is recorded while src/monitor/monitor.py:96 stores the client IP (checked). Astra: the anonymiser keeps nested session IDs and URL contents (src/analysis/anonymize_monitor_logs.py:131).

## Exit criteria
- [ ] History purged on GitHub (force-push of the rewritten main), read back: no path tests/fixtures/reports/monitor-logs in any branch or tag
- [ ] GitHub Support sensitive-data request filed for refs/pull/*
- [ ] Production checkout reset to the new origin/main before any deploy
- [ ] Privacy notice states what is collected (IP, profile, queries), the model-provider transfer, retention and opt-out scope
- [ ] DPO consulted on whether the exposure must be declared; answer recorded here
- [ ] Anonymiser drops nested identifiers and URL parameters; a test proves it; the published anonymised archive re-checked
